#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427503} :activity/id #uuid "0974eb57-6659-54d9-be86-ddfa7868dbe6" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048206 :topic/id #uuid "8850e3a0-f2fb-5671-843a-13422a22aa79" :topic/math-academy-id 4387} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427502 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13902432-1e15-5d83-9e31-77ea1c9ecb88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/9a/9a87c5ea8ceaa8a64e30b6375a8bcaa58182ac2e97d68b44c70a0a964c4727dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284963} {:answer/id #uuid "2fc8b5e0-b1db-5812-b923-c8b2aed030ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/34/340f534cb7548f2e5fcffb6153d45fd327b414aa17247bcde00b5396d24830a4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285222} {:answer/id #uuid "95737d26-61bc-5532-92fe-b8144479975c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/32/3274c0747b72b6b8ce457f20cd89d0f7d951c8a3bd138c9061448c1bedb42b55.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286146} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d0322b-eee5-55b7-919c-66200da95a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/82/824d176d4d041be340eb786ff53f8b5a352edca3ad928fc593b9799f2cc4008b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286456} {:answer/id #uuid "ed33c550-8d8c-5c22-8aed-eb90798b7c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/b6/b676b2201a4fe4d57cb005eb9527f429068eae4d18c55496ebabf9390fc19219.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286962}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284963} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc5ac333-7088-55b5-8dff-47ad3124a244" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8eb13b5c-5049-574a-9dd7-f6e99016a3c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-182001" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=Z\\times [-1,0]$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=Z\\times [-1,0]\n$$\n\n \ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a integer number and whose $y$-coordinate belongs to $[-1,0].$\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in Z,\\,y\\in [-1,0]\\}\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S,$ consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is in $[-1,0].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}=\\{(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,0]\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/63/63199d9f35c331339e97ad3b2094a520d1fb6a9892bd0beac83538c43b9e2748.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is in $[-1,0].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/03/03a6a90b3eff572ceed341de55a0d5e625e338ca18f2ae8ee85eed3bb5278167.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-3},{S}_{-2},{S}_{0},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product consists of the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\times N & =…{S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}… \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in Z}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $Z\\times [-1,0]$ as the set of vertical lines shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/9a/9a87c5ea8ceaa8a64e30b6375a8bcaa58182ac2e97d68b44c70a0a964c4727dd.png)"} :step/id #uuid "2f868252-f8e0-5a5f-92f0-b020aafff313" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427506}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427503 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389797 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c00cf5df-4240-5b04-850f-1b4b0d6f8ae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c8/c87871c50b343792c73fc18dfe92bc2065b18ed3de1e7bb70324b8b43d027206.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389799} {:answer/id #uuid "1f633a02-8088-56db-88c2-7889ba264321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/39/39db7bc1b259b222a2365441babc3421101961ea26a7143af14b526ba7f81200.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389800} {:answer/id #uuid "6c189e68-bec8-518b-a64d-56fe2a4c4033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ec/ec0e1df36bf5d93b8cdbcc3d14cd510fbe299b929ed3d19f4d901f4461093305.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389801} {:answer/id #uuid "f10813b1-b163-59a5-a38f-0b5b4e7dded5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f9/f90de7c6d88b187af3604912a647620fb88d4833e08fd086cf1a9daae52f331f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389802} {:answer/id #uuid "81b3b685-552f-53ef-8556-c54cf7663b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/86/8627676ae3b7bcdeff423d79d7289d1d3f9243e0cc69d4f3ac7d3e5c51141fc1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389803}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389800} :answer-field/id #uuid "f376ba00-5dab-590e-a791-4441f99a66cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "60baa69f-bbf2-5905-831d-ab5e879fa2f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-177648" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,1].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0,0.5]\\times [0,1]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,0.5],b\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(0.5,0),$ $(0.5,1),$ and $(0,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/5b/5b882f3fb0e7b44eb2df3a510260574e5c4a4d85842a9c0d65515f1a40894756.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,1]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,i],b\\in [0,1]\\}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(i,0),$ $(i,1),$ and $(0,1).$\n\n![](images/cb/cb530698591dbd71a8058d9faa0c60b636dc654f21e92d65ec8295aeaa67355a.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the line segment $\\{0\\}\\times [0,1]:$\n\n![](images/70/704f8f6f0666d09bb2b8a25eab0548c3eb808e2c9d394d2ae873de35cb0112d1.png)"} :step/id #uuid "49fb4645-c2a9-59e2-8599-72cac0d3d4bc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427504}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427504 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389916 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1204bd88-b470-5b91-b7c2-a8d4ad537898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/46/463ae2387423a48dd557af8cfd9b01b6bc08b95f1b3c2f337c6b0c53d3731fa2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389918} {:answer/id #uuid "60caae02-3071-514b-9258-9f96b6664d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/2d/2df87b90d770a5f2c0ba40a55330409d1cd80866b7e34299eab6dcbf675c6a13.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389919} {:answer/id #uuid "746ae67c-caa3-593c-9e3f-51831b036f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f7/f7e54dd973126e3179e79b1ba1a26f4a7c1c541ca764b14c4ccef73b4452509e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389920} {:answer/id #uuid "c89a44bf-6d27-578e-9136-6babbb95e931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/2f/2f28e6f8c8e6e9fa13b5285e25e5460d26548ffd9d71077d1c6073e6c4c743a1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389921} {:answer/id #uuid "51564c2b-bcad-5e6e-9c34-dbd7a16d3a00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/58/5888cf137eea674995b4c9cc37285b4130df5de3a2a2fa63b1b5b195910526c1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389922}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389920} :answer-field/id #uuid "c241a74d-c7f4-5b96-a451-f6a50f08f04a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6bae802a-d591-53eb-b628-21b012d03cee" :question/math-academy-id "q-181968" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={Z}^{-}\\times N$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS={Z}^{-}\\times N\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a negative integer and whose $y$-coordinate is a natural number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,y\\in N\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}=\\{(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in N\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/8e/8e6816767cd2010fca1b8991ed9c5e0c42d3a6d6466d78025534bc8362a174b9.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{-2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-2}=\\{(-2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in N\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/4d/4d0fe261e790520e6a8786e6f024d5b9cb7cd54c18242103a1f4b77f09653abc.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-5},{S}_{-4},{S}_{-3}$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =…{S}_{-4}\\cup {S}_{-3}\\cup {S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1} \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in {Z}^{-}}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize ${Z}^{-}\\times N$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/f7/f7e54dd973126e3179e79b1ba1a26f4a7c1c541ca764b14c4ccef73b4452509e.png)"} :step/id #uuid "7ffe2ddd-605f-5cd8-bf11-9de23847ac5f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427505}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427505 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198806 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a224de-0a7a-5ebf-83b7-7575ba7f49c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f8/f8eb09869ae1733a58ed488cc747bca4dddf56ebc0da0de53ff21a2181208217.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284846} {:answer/id #uuid "72e2efff-69aa-52bb-a78c-e682719225d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/30/30c98beaaaf9728a31685195cd236464ceba34094aeda381838f33ba2a134b4c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285846} {:answer/id #uuid "ca095e46-57a5-5045-9532-8b19c4502e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/82/8210684df0b5143b3b51a3a30cd03e4cdbc4bb80d139c25385dd0fde668d6fd4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286632} {:answer/id #uuid "d08d3be0-ab3c-598f-b81f-c0a937f9bb66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ee/ee6ac65885afc561a40d51352bb6a4eac4974db27274cb35ad3032b7a7a8ffb4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286686} {:answer/id #uuid "efd1c7f0-4319-573c-83f6-fc4b435b4a82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c2/c2474d727fe1d97a21f67e9c4ae71b19dcc98106bb7b34c3ccef19ae56b44487.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286987}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286632} :answer-field/id #uuid "39cb9311-07e3-5d93-89a4-7c78cbd6de5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "10624e27-fb3c-5852-bfb2-5c112258247b" :question/math-academy-id "q-181984" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the set $S=[-1,1]\\times [0,1]$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=[-1,1]\\times [0,1]\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1].$\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,1],\\,y\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}=\\{(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [0,1]\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/1c/1cc30fcc7543bfbbf8c5c59d1436eb3b1a0799d60c9ad1d899957e8fd17d58ab.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in [-1,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}=\\{(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [0,1]\\}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in [-1,1],$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i,1).$\n\n![](images/49/494c9d77b0ff339b90792270c9d641054a03a2918e3c56a93747b42a77ee3ccf.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $I=[-1,1]:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following rectangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/7c/7c5ac5dad0aaacb4347c260d634e6bcd2d6102b25d51813fe106803417cc7539.png)"} :step/id #uuid "8cd3cbad-1220-514c-ad2e-d949f26d97ee" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427502}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427506 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427501 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b353f4d-b6c1-544c-a565-cbc81d0130e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/49/4928c291f6eb42646dd9623b7c665a1569462b1b5ce19b31501ae3c655303b87.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427495} {:answer/id #uuid "89fe3c93-58d2-564c-8818-f614741ab1a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/ff/ffaa9807fa5155dcc848d68bed93a16b267045fae3f5d4d0945e064ad5c11eef.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427496} {:answer/id #uuid "99bf3628-2a02-53d8-922c-2471074f7424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/0a/0a655218c2ee2a93e2c37601b8d989f449395270fbea8ff2dda34caedccd95e1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427497} {:answer/id #uuid "9a8e4cd5-94f1-51c7-aff4-ee1d59197f9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/f1/f15dd410cc7b5e47cd246182606ef7e9fb5c51caae792815104ab788d0da9a48.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427498} {:answer/id #uuid "d3489613-d07f-57e1-bd54-7d15cf117eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/bf/bf3963dc09b844714f7cbe85e93caf539b2de64cd6a5264d9a7477e724ea5a8b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427499}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427496} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5e7343a-4633-545d-a3b9-3c2ada585e3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "46ba7fa0-d231-5401-8252-d4e156d84cf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-184533" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,2]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times [-1,1].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}=[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [-1,1],b\\in [-1,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(-1,-1),$ $(-1,1),$ $(1,1),$ and $(1,-1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/71/712970edb9966d6544cbe4a360aaa0de3436f356c4c7f23ff601c70ef168a521.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times [-1,1]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [-i,i],b\\in [-1,1]\\}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(-i,-1),$ $(-i,1),$ $(i,1),$ and $(i,-1).$\n\n![](images/68/68f8c51062bd9d3ecadd33b0a67ea0990f631375aba9f9cc705946c79abf47d0.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the line segment $\\{0\\}\\times [-1,1]:$\n\n![](images/ff/ffaa9807fa5155dcc848d68bed93a16b267045fae3f5d4d0945e064ad5c11eef.png)"} :step/id #uuid "c27fb01c-6abc-53a8-9ed3-81896b8737cf"}] :activity/title "Visualizing Cartesian Products" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427494}]}
